#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:19
msgid ""
"Recording data from inside your own code gives you more control than using "
"the command line alone. This article shows how to use the ``rosbag2_py`` "
"Python API to write received and generated data to bags. After following "
"this tutorial, you can record topic data, synthetic data, and timestamped "
"samples from Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:27
msgid "**Goal:** Record data from your own Python node to a bag."
msgstr ""

