#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:335
msgid "4 Record synthetic data from a node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:337
msgid ""
"Any data can be recorded into a bag, not just data received over a topic. A "
"common use case for writing to a bag from your own node is to generate and "
"store synthetic data. In this section you will learn how to write a node "
"that generates some data and stores it in a bag. We will demonstrate two "
"approaches for doing this. The first uses a node with a timer; this is the "
"approach that you would use if your data generation is external to the node, "
"such as reading data directly from hardware (e.g. a camera). The second "
"approach does not use a node; this is the approach you can use when you do "
"not need to use any functionality from the ROS infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:345
msgid "4.1 Write a Python node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:347
msgid ""
"Inside the ``ros2_ws/src/bag_recorder_nodes_py/bag_recorder_nodes_py`` "
"directory, create a new file called ``data_generator_node.py`` and paste the "
"following code into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:349
msgid ""
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.executors import ExternalShutdownException\n"
"from rclpy.node import Node\n"
"from rclpy.serialization import serialize_message\n"
"from example_interfaces.msg import Int32\n"
"\n"
"import rosbag2_py\n"
"\n"
"class DataGeneratorNode(Node):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__('data_generator_node')\n"
"        self.data = Int32()\n"
"        self.data.data = 0\n"
"        self.writer = rosbag2_py.SequentialWriter()\n"
"\n"
"        storage_options = rosbag2_py.StorageOptions(\n"
"            uri='timed_synthetic_bag',\n"
"            storage_id='mcap')\n"
"        converter_options = rosbag2_py.ConverterOptions('', '')\n"
"        self.writer.open(storage_options, converter_options)\n"
"\n"
"        topic_info = rosbag2_py.TopicMetadata(\n"
"            id=0,\n"
"            name='synthetic',\n"
"            type='example_interfaces/msg/Int32',\n"
"            serialization_format='cdr')\n"
"        self.writer.create_topic(topic_info)\n"
"\n"
"        self.timer = self.create_timer(1, self.timer_callback)\n"
"\n"
"    def timer_callback(self):\n"
"        self.writer.write(\n"
"            'synthetic',\n"
"            serialize_message(self.data),\n"
"            self.get_clock().now().nanoseconds)\n"
"        self.data.data += 1\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def main(args=None):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        with rclpy.init(args=args):\n"
"            dgn = DataGeneratorNode()\n"
"            rclpy.spin(dgn)\n"
"    except (KeyboardInterrupt, ExternalShutdownException):\n"
"        pass\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:402
msgid "4.2 Examine the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:404
msgid ""
"Much of this code is the same as the first example. The important "
"differences are described here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:407
msgid "First, the name of the bag is changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:409
msgid ""
"storage_options = rosbag2_py.StorageOptions(\n"
"    uri='timed_synthetic_bag',\n"
"    storage_id='mcap')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:415
msgid "The name of the topic is also changed, as is the data type stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:417
msgid ""
"topic_info = rosbag2_py.TopicMetadata(\n"
"    id=0,\n"
"    name='synthetic',\n"
"    type='example_interfaces/msg/Int32',\n"
"    serialization_format='cdr')\n"
"self.writer.create_topic(topic_info)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:426
msgid ""
"Rather than a subscription to a topic, this node has a timer. The timer "
"fires with a one-second period, and calls the given member function when it "
"does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:429
msgid "self.timer = self.create_timer(1, self.timer_callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:433
msgid ""
"Within the timer callback, we generate (or otherwise obtain, e.g. read from "
"a serial port connected to some hardware) the data we wish to store in the "
"bag. As with the previous example, the data is not yet serialized, so we "
"must serialize it before passing it to the writer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:436
msgid ""
"self.writer.write(\n"
"    'synthetic',\n"
"    serialize_message(self.data),\n"
"    self.get_clock().now().nanoseconds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Recording-A-Bag-From-Your-Own-Node-Py.rst:444
msgid "4.3 Add executable"
